@page "/getting-started/templates"

<DocPage Eyebrow="Guide"
         Title="Project Templates"
         Lede="Start a new BlazOrbit project from a `dotnet new` template — Server or WebAssembly, .NET 8 or .NET 10, with optional localization wired up.">

    <section class="doc-section">
        <h2 class="doc-section__title">1. Install the templates</h2>
        <p class="doc-section__description">
            The templates ship as a single NuGet package. Install once and the
            <code>dotnet new</code> CLI picks them up globally.
        </p>

        <BOBCodeBlock Title="Terminal"
                      Language="SyntaxHighlightLanguage.CSharp"
                      Code="dotnet new install BlazOrbit.Templates" />

        <p class="doc-section__description">
            Update to a newer release at any time:
        </p>

        <BOBCodeBlock Title="Terminal"
                      Language="SyntaxHighlightLanguage.CSharp"
                      Code="dotnet new install BlazOrbit.Templates::*" />

        <p class="doc-section__description">
            Uninstall when you no longer need them:
        </p>

        <BOBCodeBlock Title="Terminal"
                      Language="SyntaxHighlightLanguage.CSharp"
                      Code="dotnet new uninstall BlazOrbit.Templates" />
    </section>

    <section class="doc-section">
        <h2 class="doc-section__title">2. Available templates</h2>
        <p class="doc-section__description">
            Both templates ship the same component surface and theming pipeline.
            Pick the hosting model that fits your app.
        </p>

        <table class="doc-table">
            <thead>
                <tr>
                    <th>Short name</th>
                    <th>Hosting</th>
                    <th>Description</th>
                </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
                <tr>
                    <td><code>blazorbit-server</code></td>
                    <td>Blazor Server</td>
                    <td>Interactive Server render mode + cookie-friendly auth integration points.</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td><code>blazorbit-wasm</code></td>
                    <td>Blazor WebAssembly</td>
                    <td>Standalone WASM with PWA manifest, service worker, and BlazOrbit bundles preconfigured.</td>
                </tr>
            </tbody>
        </table>
    </section>

    <section class="doc-section">
        <h2 class="doc-section__title">3. Parameters</h2>

        <table class="doc-table">
            <thead>
                <tr>
                    <th>Parameter</th>
                    <th>Values</th>
                    <th>Default</th>
                    <th>Effect</th>
                </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
                <tr>
                    <td><code>-F</code> / <code>--Framework</code></td>
                    <td><code>net8.0</code> · <code>net10.0</code></td>
                    <td><code>net8.0</code></td>
                    <td>Targets the chosen TFM and switches per-version host plumbing (e.g. <code>MapStaticAssets</code>, <code>ImportMap</code>, <code>NotFoundPage</code>).</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td><code>-IncludeLocalization</code></td>
                    <td><code>true</code> · <code>false</code></td>
                    <td><code>false</code></td>
                    <td>Adds <code>BlazOrbit.Localization.Server</code> / <code>.Wasm</code>, registers <code>RequestLocalization</code> / <code>localStorage</code> bridge, and exposes <code>BOBCultureSelector</code> in the navbar.</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td><code>-IncludeCharts</code></td>
                    <td><code>true</code> · <code>false</code></td>
                    <td><code>false</code></td>
                    <td>Adds <code>BlazOrbit.Charts</code>, registers <code>AddBlazOrbitCharts()</code>, and replaces Home with a dashboard sample.</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td><code>-UseNotificationsCenter</code></td>
                    <td><code>true</code> · <code>false</code></td>
                    <td><code>false</code></td>
                    <td>Adds <code>BlazOrbit.Notifications</code>, registers <code>AddBlazOrbitNotifications()</code>, adds <code>BOBNotificationBell</code> in the navbar, and includes a notification inbox demo in Home.</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td><code>-UseHotKeys</code></td>
                    <td><code>true</code> · <code>false</code></td>
                    <td><code>false</code></td>
                    <td>Adds <code>BlazOrbit.Hotkeys</code>, registers <code>AddBlazOrbitHotkeys()</code>, mounts <code>BOBHotkeyHost</code> in the app shell, and includes a keyboard-shortcuts demo in Home.</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td><code>-Theme</code></td>
                    <td><code>None</code> · <code>NeoBrutalism</code> · <code>BentoGrid</code> · <code>Glassmorphism</code> · <code>FlatDesign</code> · <code>MaterialDesign</code> · <code>Neomorphism</code> · <code>Claymorphism</code> · <code>RetroWeb</code></td>
                    <td><code>None</code></td>
                    <td>Pre-built visual theme that overrides the default palette and design tokens (border radius, border width, input radius, font family, etc.).</td>
                </tr>
            </tbody>
        </table>
    </section>

    <section class="doc-section">
        <h2 class="doc-section__title">4. Generate a project</h2>

        <p class="doc-section__description">
            <strong>Blazor Server, .NET 10, no localization:</strong>
        </p>
        <BOBCodeBlock Title="Terminal"
                      Language="SyntaxHighlightLanguage.CSharp"
                      Code="dotnet new blazorbit-server -n MyApp -F net10.0" />

        <p class="doc-section__description" style="margin-top: 1.5rem;">
            <strong>Blazor Server, .NET 10, with localization:</strong>
        </p>
        <BOBCodeBlock Title="Terminal"
                      Language="SyntaxHighlightLanguage.CSharp"
                      Code="dotnet new blazorbit-server -n MyApp -F net10.0 -IncludeLocalization true" />

        <p class="doc-section__description" style="margin-top: 1.5rem;">
            <strong>Blazor WebAssembly, .NET 8, no localization:</strong>
        </p>
        <BOBCodeBlock Title="Terminal"
                      Language="SyntaxHighlightLanguage.CSharp"
                      Code="dotnet new blazorbit-wasm -n MyApp -F net8.0" />

        <p class="doc-section__description" style="margin-top: 1.5rem;">
            <strong>Blazor WebAssembly, .NET 10, with localization:</strong>
        </p>
        <BOBCodeBlock Title="Terminal"
                      Language="SyntaxHighlightLanguage.CSharp"
                      Code="dotnet new blazorbit-wasm -n MyApp -F net10.0 -IncludeLocalization true" />

        <p class="doc-section__description" style="margin-top: 1.5rem;">
            <strong>Blazor Server, .NET 10, with Neo-Brutalism theme:</strong>
        </p>
        <BOBCodeBlock Title="Terminal"
                      Language="SyntaxHighlightLanguage.CSharp"
                      Code="dotnet new blazorbit-server -n MyApp -F net10.0 -Theme NeoBrutalism" />

        <p class="doc-section__description" style="margin-top: 1.5rem;">
            <strong>Blazor Server, .NET 10, with everything:</strong>
        </p>
        <BOBCodeBlock Title="Terminal"
                      Language="SyntaxHighlightLanguage.CSharp"
                      Code="dotnet new blazorbit-server -n MyApp -F net10.0 -IncludeLocalization true -IncludeCharts true -UseNotificationsCenter true -UseHotKeys true" />

        <div class="doc-callout doc-callout--info">
            <span class="doc-callout__icon">ℹ️</span>
            <div>
                Run <code>cd MyApp &amp;&amp; dotnet run</code> to launch. The default Home page is a
                live showcase of the component library you can edit at
                <code>Components/Pages/Home.razor</code> (Server) or <code>Pages/Home.razor</code> (WASM).
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="doc-section">
        <h2 class="doc-section__title">5. What the template ships</h2>
        <p class="doc-section__description">Out of the box, every generated project includes:</p>
        <ul>
            <li>A pre-wired <code>BOBInitializer</code> in <code>MainLayout.razor</code> with theme switching and the modal/toast hosts.</li>
            <li>A branded loading screen using the BlazOrbit icon, replaced once the interactive shell mounts.</li>
            <li>The CSS bundle linked from <code>_content/BlazOrbit/css/blazorbit.css</code> and the anti-flash bootstrap script.</li>
            <li>A favicon set (SVG + 48/192/512 PNG) and, on WASM, a PWA manifest.</li>
            <li>A showcase Home page demonstrating buttons, inputs, cards, and accordion with palette-driven styling.</li>
            <li>When localization is enabled: <code>BOBCultureSelector</code> in the navbar, <code>en-US</code> / <code>es-ES</code> / <code>fr-FR</code> sample cultures, and the request-localization wiring.</li>
            <li>When charts are enabled: <code>BlazOrbit.Charts</code> package, <code>AddBlazOrbitCharts()</code> registration, and a dashboard Home page with sample KPIs and data visualizations.</li>
            <li>When notifications are enabled: <code>BOBNotificationBell</code> in the navbar and a sample inbox with push / mark-read / remove demo.</li>
            <li>When hotkeys are enabled: <code>BOBHotkeyHost</code> in the layout shell and a sample shortcuts table with <code>Ctrl+K</code> / <code>Ctrl+F1</code> handlers.</li>
        </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="doc-section">
        <h2 class="doc-section__title">For contributors — local feed</h2>
        <p class="doc-section__description">
            Validating template changes against unreleased library bits requires a
            local NuGet feed. The repo ships a script that packs the libraries plus
            the templates package, installs them, generates a matrix of sample
            projects, and builds each combo end-to-end.
        </p>

        <BOBCodeBlock Title="Terminal"
                      Language="SyntaxHighlightLanguage.CSharp"
                      Code="./scripts/test-templates.ps1" />

        <p class="doc-section__description">
            See <code>scripts/test-templates.ps1 -Help</code> for flags
            (<code>-SkipBlazOrbitPack</code>, <code>-KeepWorkDir</code>, custom <code>-Matrix</code>, …).
        </p>
    </section>
</DocPage>
